# Reviewer-owned structure-budget grants: `<path> <n>` per line. A trailing `/`
# on the path makes a directory file-count budget. Use exact paths only, because
# each grant is a named decision.
# A file line-count grant has headroom of about 15 percent: it is the actual
# line count of the file on the grant date, multiplied by 1.15 and rounded up.
# Thus small growth does not need a new reviewer decision. Growth past the grant
# needs one. A directory file-count grant is an exact cap, and the next file in
# that directory needs a new decision. A path with no grant keeps the default
# limit.
# Gate fragments + contract runner; granted 2026-07-02 (dry-structure-cleanup).
.bench/ 13

